# Motion Design Rules

## Library and imports

- Use `motion` (Motion for React), not `framer-motion`.
- Import from `motion/react`: `import { motion, MotionConfig, AnimatePresence, useReducedMotion } from "motion/react"`.
- Wrap the app in `<MotionConfig reducedMotion="user">` so transform/layout animations are disabled for users who request reduced motion while opacity/color transitions remain.
- Use `useReducedMotion()` for bespoke cases where a transform must be replaced by a fade.
- Keep imports tree-shakeable; never import the whole library namespace.

## Motion tokens

| Token | Value | Use |
|---|---|---|
| `--ease-out-expo` | `cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1)` | entrances, reveals |
| `--ease-standard` | `cubic-bezier(0.2, 0, 0, 1)` | UI state changes |
| `--duration-fast` | 140ms | hover, focus, press |
| `--duration-base` | 240ms | drawers, cards, nav |
| `--duration-slow` | 420ms | section reveal |
| stagger | 40-60ms | lists, cards, text lines |

- Animate only `transform` and `opacity` by default. Avoid `width`, `height`, `top`, `left`, `filter`, and `box-shadow` in loops.
- Springs are for direct manipulation (drag, tap, 3D settle), not page-load choreography.
- No bounce/overshoot on text or controls.
- Use `whileInView` with `viewport={{ once: true, amount: 0.25 }}`; do not re-trigger on every scroll.
- Use `layout`/`layoutId` only when a shared element genuinely changes position.
- Use `AnimatePresence` for removable UI and ensure exit animations do not delay focus restoration.

## Accessibility

- Never autoplay carousels, video, or ambient loops.
- Never hijack scroll. No parallax on large surfaces.
- Reduced motion: replace x/y/scale transitions with opacity, disable auto-rotation, stop infinite loops, and pause 3D rendering.
- Motion must not be the only signal for state, success, or error.
- Keep focus outlines visible during and after animation.
- No flashing above 3 Hz.

## Performance

- Keep above-the-fold entrance work under 420ms and avoid long tasks over 50ms.
- Use CSS transitions for simple hover/focus; use Motion for orchestration, gestures, and layout.
- Pause animations when the tab is hidden or the element is offscreen.
- Avoid animating large blurred layers; blur plus transform is expensive.
- Test on a mid-tier Android profile with 4x CPU throttling.

## Anti-patterns

- Scroll-jacking, pinned sections that trap the user, or forced full-page transitions.
- Infinite floating/rotating decoration around text.
- Animating layout properties on every scroll frame.
- Using motion to hide slow loading or missing content.
- `transition-all` on interactive elements.

